Input: The population size: N
Output: The final population  \( P_{t} \) 

1 Initialize a main population  \( MP_{1} \)  with size N/2;
2 Initialize an auxiliary population  \( AP_{1} \)  with size N/2;
3 Initialize a record queue  \( MR_{1} \)  with size N/2 for main population;
4 Initialize a record queue  \( AR_{1} \)  with size N/2 for auxiliary population;
5  \( t \leftarrow 1 \) ;
6 while  \( t \leq T_{max} \)  do
7    /* Produce offspring populations  \( MO_{t} \)  and  \( AO_{t} \)  according to Algorithm 2. */
8    ( \( MP_{t}, MO_{t}, MR_{t} \) ) ← Algorithm 2( \( MP_{t}, MR_{t} \) );
9    ( \( AP_{t}, AO_{t}, AR_{t} \) ) ← Algorithm 2( \( AP_{t}, AR_{t} \) );
10    /* Perform cooperation between the main and auxiliary populations. */
11    \( MP_{t} \leftarrow MP_{t} \cup MO_{t} \cup AO_{t} \) ;
12    \( AP_{t} \leftarrow AP_{t} \cup MO_{t} \cup AO_{t} \) ;
13    \( MP_{t} \leftarrow \)  the best N/2 individuals in  \( MP_{t} \)  according to CDP;
14    \( AP_{t} \leftarrow \)  the best N/2 individuals in  \( AP_{t} \)  according to the  \( \epsilon \)  method;
15    \( t \leftarrow t + 1 \) ;
16 end
17  \( P_{t} \leftarrow MP_{t} \cup AP_{t} \) ;
18 return  \( P_{t} \)

