Input: An inputted population: \(\mathbb{IP}_t\), an inputted record queue: \(\mathbb{IR}_t\)

Output: The inputted population: \(\mathbb{IP}_t\), the offspring population: \(\mathbb{IO}_t\), the updated record set: \(\mathbb{IR}_t\)

1. \(\mathbb{IO}_t = \emptyset\);

2 for \(i \leftarrow 1\) to \(\|\mathbb{IP}_t\|\) do

3 if \(1 - \frac{t}{T_{max}} < rand\) then

4 \(F^b \leftarrow\) a value regarding the DE control parameter randomly generated from [0, 1];

5 \(M^b \leftarrow\) a mutation type randomly selected from PL;

6 else

7 \(r^b \leftarrow\) a record with the maximum cosine value with \(x^i\);

8 \(F^b \leftarrow\) the value regarding the DE control parameter in \(r^i\);

9 \(M^b \leftarrow\) the mutation type in \(r^i\);

10 end

11 \(x^{c1}, x^{c2}, x^{c3} \leftarrow\) three randomly selected individuals from \(\mathbb{IP}_t\);

12 \(x^* \leftarrow\) a new individual generated by \(x^i, x^{c1}, x^{c2}\), and \(x^{c3}\) with \(F^b\) according to Eq.(25);

13 Fix \(x^*\) back to the boundary constraints;

14 \(x^* \leftarrow\) the individual obtained by performing the \(M^b\)-th mutation operation to \(x^*\) according to Eqs .(26)-(29);

15 Fix \(x^*\) back to the boundary constraints;

16 \(c^*, v^* \leftarrow\) the constraint violation degree of \(x^*\) and the objectives value of \(x^*\);

17 \(\mathbb{IO}_t \leftarrow \mathbb{IO}_t \cup x^*\);

18 \(r^* \leftarrow \{x^*, c^*, v^*, F^b, M^b\}\);

19 if \(x^*\) is better than \(x^i\) then

20 \(\mathbb{IR}_t \leftarrow\) the updated record obtained by adding \(r^*\) into \(\mathbb{IR}_t\) while removing a record from it according to FIFO;

21 end

22 end

23 return \(\mathbb{IP}_t, \mathbb{IO}_t, \mathbb{IR}_t\)
